  "slug": "builder-capsid-20a5",
  "summary": "Updated and new open-source in silico tools now cover primer specificity, pocket-based virtual screening, and CRISPR base editing design.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is in silico pre-experimental evaluation: software that encodes explicit sequence, geometric, or pharmacological criteria and reports outcomes before wet-lab work. AssayBLAST v2 extends in silico primer and probe evaluation with strand and proximity checks, amplification outcome estimation, and adaptive BLAST parameter tuning. The flavivirus workflow chains Concavity pocket detection, docking-to-Kd conversion, SwissADME integration, and LE, LLE and FQ scoring into a reproducible, open-source pipeline. BEstimate applies the same logic to CRISPR base editing, predicting on- and off-target activity for gRNA design and annotating installed edits. The items are heterogeneous and share the design-and-evaluate pattern rather than a common target class. What is new is the emphasis on reproducibility and explicit reporting of intermediate criteria, such as strand checks, ligand efficiency metrics, and off-target annotation, within single, freely available tools.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-04-30"
}
